  "id": "DrugBank_DB01289 - MONDO_5148",
  "verbalization": "Glisoxepide, a drug with a known indication for diabetes mellitus, exhibits a synergistic interaction with Gliclazide and Clorobiocin, both of which are indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus. This suggests that Glisoxepide may enhance the therapeutic effect of these drugs in the context of diabetes management. The presence of a synergistic interaction between Glisoxepide and Gliclazide, a well-established antidiabetic agent, implies that Glisoxepide could potentially augment the antidiabetic activity of Gliclazide, thereby contributing to improved glycemic control. The evidence from multiple paths supports a mechanistic link between Glisoxepide and Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, particularly through its interaction with Gliclazide, which is a key component in the treatment of the condition. The integration of these findings suggests that Glisoxepide may act as a potential adjunct in the management of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, though further investigation is needed to confirm its efficacy and safety in clinical settings.",
